                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Dark Grim Mariupolis creates a point and click adventure branch of it's own with it's interesting theme and dialogue. Aside from the mythology, mysticismm, and pseudo-dystopian society world you can easily found yourself wrapped up in interest as you control the footsteps of Thor in this crime noir adventure. Aside from the two color simple yet elegant art style and intriguing story line this game really excels with excellent sound design. The pattering of the rain combined with the calm yet unsettling smooth background music sets the tone as you are playing a pseudo-detective role. \n\nThere will be plenty of times this title will have you scratching your head in thought, but that's a good thing. The puzzles on this game come off as complicated but they are solvable by looking in the correct place. You may have to revert back to a book in a previous building. The games puzzles are actually designed very intelligently in some of these texts. If you get stuck in a particular area, there is a clue button in the top corner. The deeper you dive into the lore and texts of the world, the more surrealistic it seems to become. The game also does a great job of letting you know once a section is complete by making particular characters leave. This is helpful if you backtrack into an empty building; because you know your job is done there. \n\nAlthough the puzzles are intelligent they may seem to cryptic at times. The devs are helpful to give feedback so that's a plus. The only other real problems I had with this title aren't major things. The ui navigation took a bit longer than it felt like it should have to get used to. Once you get used to it, it's fine. Sometimes the walking speed was a bit slower that I would have liked (looking at you bar entrance). Lastly I noticed taking a screenshot would seem to soft freeze the game for a moment. \n\n[h1]Pros[/h1]\n+Dark and interesting atmosphere\n+Witty and intelligent dialogue and characters\n+Cross area puzzles\n+Original art style with excellent sound design\n+Helpful community and developers\n\n[h1]Cons[/h1]\n-Intelligence in puzzles is almost a bit too cryptic at times\n-Somewhat confusing ui navigation at first\n-Walking speed can be slow at times\n-Taking screenshots will soft freeze the game for a moment\n\nThis title will take you around three to four hours unguided. Possibly less if you are extremely good at point and click adventure games. The art, sound, characters, and story are original enough for me to warrant a recommendation for this title. You will get something a bit different than most titles with this one, and a low price of five dollars is pretty good for the experience.\n\n[quote=Crimson-Albedo]Follow my reviews through my curator at [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/32482033/]Crim's Humble Opinion[/url][/quote]",
